  <title>SQL window</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>SQL window</gui></guiseq> runs a
  query typed in SQL and shows the result as a table, for questions no report
  answers.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Type the query and click <gui>Run SQL</gui>. The time it took is
    shown; an error is shown in place of the table. A blank cell in the table
    is a NULL, and a true/false column shows a NULL unticked.</p></item>
    <item><p>To keep what a query changes, tick <gui>Commit</gui> before
    clicking <gui>Run SQL</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To keep a query, type a name for it in the box at the top and
    click <gui>Save SQL</gui>. Choose a saved query from the box to load it
    again; right click the box and choose <gui>Delete</gui> to remove
    one.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <note><p>Unless <gui>Commit</gui> is ticked, everything run here is rolled
  back afterwards: a query that changes data reports how many rows it would
  have affected, but changes nothing. With <gui>Commit</gui> ticked, a query
  that succeeds is kept at once and cannot be undone here. A query that fails
  is always rolled back. <gui>Commit</gui> is unticked each time the window
  opens.</p></note>

  <p><gui>Report hub</gui> exports the result; see <link
  xref="report_hub"/>. The last query run is kept as <gui>Current</gui>.</p>

</page>
